I am trying to create a Verilog model for a sequence generator. It must meet the following specifications:
	- Inputs:
		- Clock
		- Active-low reset
		- Enable
	- Outputs:
		- Data (8 bits)

While enabled, it should generate an output sequence of the following hexadecimal values and then repeat:
	- 0xAF
	- 0xBC
	- 0xE2
	- 0x78
	- 0xFF
	- 0xE2
	- 0x0B
	- 0x8D

How would I write a design that meets these specifications?
Use module name sequence_generator with ports input clk, input reset_n,
input enable, output reg [7:0] data.
Produce the first sequence item on the first enabled rising edge after reset,
then advance once per enabled rising edge. Hold output and position while disabled;
resume from that position when enabled again. Reset restarts the sequence.


Your previous attempt:
```verilog
module sequence_generator (
    input clk,
    input reset_n,
    input enable,
    output reg [7:0] data
);

    // Define the sequence
    reg [7:0] sequence [0:7] = '{8'hAF, 8'hBC, 8'hE2, 8'h78, 8'hFF, 8'hE2, 8'h0B, 8'h8D};

    // State variables
    reg [3:0] index;
    reg [3:0] prev_index;

    // Always block for state updates
    always @(posedge clk) begin
        if (!reset_n) begin
            // Reset: restart sequence
            index <= 0;
            prev_index <= 0;
            data <= 8'h00;
        end else begin
            if (enable) begin
                // When enabled, advance the index
                if (index == 7) begin
                    index <= 0;
                end else begin
                    index <= index + 1;
                end
                // Update data
                data <= sequence[index];
            end else begin
                // When disabled, hold the current data and index
                data <= data;
                index <= index;
            end
        end
    end

endmodule

```

